//? Title: OpenPose:directed tensor fields and visible optimization
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A complete six-stage OpenPose teaching model learns confidence and directed limb fields from genuine whole COCO8-Pose photographs. Explicit SGD and Adam loops,independent target/decoder checks and all held-out images expose both the computation and its limited pose results.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/openpose_pafs.cpp`.

> The method

Construct annotation-supported confidence/PAF targets,supervise all twelve raw fields,and decode local peaks through directed line integration and conflict-safe person assembly. Numerical preprocessing,objectives,decoding,metrics and figure values use the tensor library. Containers retain only metadata,topology and presentation.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/openpose_pafs_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/openpose_pafs_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/openpose_pafs_concept.tikz > build/openpose_pafs_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/openpose_pafs_concept.svg build/openpose_pafs_concept.dvi > build/openpose_pafs_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
