> A directed field associates joints with people

Each of19 anatomical limbs has an x/y field pair. Inside its strip,the target
is the unit vector from its first joint to its second. Overlapping people
average vectors;opposing limbs can cancel. Zero-length limbs add no vector.
Joint confidence is the maximum truncated Gaussian over people. Background
is1 minus the maximum joint confidence. COCO17 becomes18 only by deriving
a neck when both shoulders are labeled. This is annotation transformation,
not an invented person or a learned joint.

Unknown joints or limbs disable their channel only inside the original
person's box. These conservative rectangles are a teaching policy;they are
not COCO crowd segmentation masks. Visibility1 and2 both supervise.
Targets use half-pixel16/128 coordinates,sigma1 and strip radius1 by default.
The fixture shows two disjoint horizontal chains and their unit directed PAF.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/openpose_pafs_targets.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  std::vector<float> metadata(2 * 18 * 3, 0.f);
  for (int p = 0; p < 2; ++p)
    for (int j : {1, 2, 3}) {
      const int at = (p * 18 + j) * 3;
      metadata[at] = j == 1 ? 19.5f : j == 2 ? 51.5f : 67.5f;
      metadata[at + 1] = p ? 91.5f : 27.5f;
      metadata[at + 2] = 2;
    }
  m::PafData d{n::zeros({1, 128, 128, 3}), n::from_vector(metadata, {1, 2, 18, 3}),
               n::full({1, 2, 4}, 16.), n::full({1}, 2., n::DType::Int32),
               n::zeros({1}, n::DType::Int32)};
  const auto t = m::PreparePafTargets(d, 16, 128, .5, .75);
  const auto decoded = m::DecodePafs(t.heatmap, t.paf, 0);
  std::print("Independent two-person fixture:{} peaks,{} directed links,{} people;reversed "
             "PAF {} people.\n",
             decoded.peaks.size(), decoded.links.size(), decoded.people.size(),
             m::DecodePafs(t.heatmap, -t.paf, 0).people.size());
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(n::select(n::select(t.heatmap, 0, 0), 2, 1), {0}), 0,
                              1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(n::select(n::select(t.paf, 0, 0), 2, 0), {0}), -1, 1);
  a.title("Two original neck confidence peaks")
      .x_label("field column")
      .y_label("field row0 at bottom");
  b.title("Directed neck-to-shoulder x field")
      .x_label("field column")
      .y_label("field row0 at bottom");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/openpose_pafs_targets.svg");
}
```
