> All six stages and both feedback branches remain connected

The VGG-shaped backbone has10 convolutions plus2 CPM convolutions and3
VALID pools. Input is BGR*(255/256)-.5. Confidence and PAF heads are linear,
unbounded19/38 channel fields. Five later stages concatenate both previous
fields with shared features,and each branch uses five7x7 then two1x1 layers.
The full network has52,311,446 learned scalars;divisor8 compact widths retain
1,217,438 scalars. Both have92 convolutions,184 learned leaves and100
retained activations. No BN,pretrained weights or person-box forward inputs.
The native suite executes full128px backward as well as compact backward.
This compact probe also checks final loss reaches both initial fields.
```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::ParameterStore p(197);
  const auto image =
      (.5 + .4 * n::sin(n::arange(0, 2 * 128 * 128 * 3) * .13)).reshape({2, 128, 128, 3});
  const auto out = m::OpenPose(p, image, 8);
  const auto final = n::mean(n::square(out.heatmaps[5])) + n::mean(n::square(out.pafs[5]));
  const auto gradients = n::grad(final, {out.heatmaps[0], out.pafs[0]});
  std::print(
      "Compact learned values {},leaves {},stages {};final-to-first confidence/PAF gradient "
      "norms {:.6f}/{:.6f}.\n| stage | confidence shape | PAF shape |\n|---:|---|---|\n",
      p.count(), p.size(), out.stages.size(), n::sqrt(n::sum(n::square(gradients[0]))).item(),
      n::sqrt(n::sum(n::square(gradients[1]))).item());
  for (int s = 0; s < 6; ++s)
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", s + 1, out.heatmaps[s].shape(), out.pafs[s].shape());
}
```
