// result_end
\caption(All9 explicit Adam updates and both directly supervised final heads. Validation selects learned parameters without using held-out labels.)
\alttext(All9 explicit Adam updates and both directly supervised final heads. Validation selects learned parameters without using held-out labels.)


\image(figures/openpose_pafs_metrics.svg)
\caption(Held-out field error and custom grouped annotated-joint precision/recall/F1 for learned,SGD-prior and empty fields. Lower field MSE does not establish useful person assembly.)
\alttext(Actual four-photograph masked field errors and grouped-joint diagnostics for three declared predictors.)

\image(figures/openpose_pafs_test.png)
\caption(All4 held-out photographs,one row each:RGB|green original skeletons|red assembled predictions|red maximum joint confidence|blue maximum PAF magnitude. Display clips and byte-rounds fields only;raw numeric predictions remain unbounded. Blank predicted overlays mean no retained groups,not hidden ground truth.)
\alttext(Four genuine held-out whole photographs with original and predicted skeletons and the actual confidence and PAF outputs.)

The selected epoch3 reduces the fixed fitting probe1.329592 to.282178,
but the learned model retains **zero person groups** on held-out images.
Its confidence MSE.044782 is also worse than empty/background.024235.
The SGD prior obtains4/116 correct joints,152 predicted joints and36 groups
against14 original people:F1.029851. Neither is a useful pose estimator here.
The actual blank learned skeleton overlays and weak fields remain visible.

> Validation and scope

The native suite checks exact full/compact parameter counts,all100 stage
shapes,every learned/RGB derivative and both feedback paths. It compares every
real target/mask value and every decoder peak,link and person subset against
the retained independent host source at two field resolutions. It verifies
missing NaNs,empty objectives,every tensor preview pixel and SGD-oracle parity.
Public Doxygen examples compile and run,and the original source workflow
also executes its full model checks and three-epoch fit.

This is an8-photograph,from-scratch compact demonstration. Source dependence,
rectangular missing-label masks,one validation photograph and a coarse16px
field limit conclusions. Training loss reduction is not evidence of useful
pose accuracy;the displayed actual held-out grouping results govern that claim.

> Conclusion

The report preserves the full six-stage graph and shows every fitted update. Genuine held-out photographs and custom grouped-joint diagnostics expose the difference between reducing field loss and recovering people. This small compact experiment supports implementation checks,not benchmark accuracy or realtime claims.

> References

- [Cao et al.(2017),Realtime Multi-Person2D Pose Estimation using Part Affinity Fields](https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.08050).
- [Official COCO OpenPose deployment graph](https://github.com/CMU-Perceptual-Computing-Lab/openpose/blob/master/models/pose/coco/pose_deploy_linevec.prototxt).
- [Official COCO8-Pose dataset configuration](https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/blob/main/ultralytics/cfg/datasets/coco8-pose.yaml).
- [Lin et al.(2014),Microsoft COCO:Common Objects in Context](https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0312).
